      "id": "problem",
      "section": "problem",
      "layout": "big-statement",
      "duration_s": 10.4,
      "narration": "You creep through a dark cave and step into a pit. In the classic game, that one wrong step ends the hunt, and you can't do anything about it.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "kinetic_headline",
          "text": "One wrong step into a pit shouldn't end the whole hunt",
          "animation": "word-by-word"
        }
      ],
      "transition_in": "fade"
    },
    {
      "id": "solution",
      "section": "solution",
      "layout": "big-statement",
      "duration_s": 11.7,
      "narration": "Hunt the Wumpus remakes the 1973 cave game in Unity. Now a hazard starts a trivia duel, with a question a language model writes on the spot.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "kinetic_headline",
          "text": "Hazards start a trivia duel instead of ending the game",
          "animation": "word-by-word"
        }
      ],
      "transition_in": "slide"
    },
    {
      "id": "demo1",
      "section": "demo",
      "layout": "full-frame",
      "duration_s": 8.9,
      "narration": "The hex map of the 30-room cave. Colour tells you about your room, and text warns of neighbouring rooms, like a smell of wumpus.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "clip",
